This patch fixes the "import corrupts existing academic data" bug.
It touches two files:

  1. Code.gs                 (Google Apps Script backend / Google Sheets source of truth)
  2. house-tracker.html      (front-end display + academic aggregation)

Apply manually or use:  git apply import-fix.patch
----------------------------------------------------------------------

=== FILE 1: Code.gs ===

### 1) New sanitizer helpers (inserted just above "// ===== ENTRIES =====")

  +// ===== SANITIZERS =====
  +// Coerce any value to a finite number. null/undefined/empty/'-'/NaN -> 0.
  +function toNumber(v) {
  +  if (v === null || v === undefined || v === '') return 0;
  +  const n = Number(v);
  +  return isNaN(n) ? 0 : n;
  +}
  +function cleanEntry(raw) { ... coerces id/house/category/position/points/event/note/date/exam }
  +function cleanStudent(raw) { ... coerces name/house/cls/sec/subjects/total/exam/date }

  Purpose: reject null/undefined/empty-string/NaN/'-' values before writing, so a bad
  spreadsheet cell can never replace a valid number with empty data.

### 2) addEntries() — sanitise each row and skip entries without a valid house

    - sheet.appendRow([id, entry.house, entry.category, entry.subCategory||'', entry.position||0,
    -                  entry.points, entry.event||'', entry.note||'', date, entry.exam||'']);
    + const entry = cleanEntry(raw);
    + if(!entry.house) { skipped++; Logger.log(...); return; }
    + sheet.appendRow([entry.id, entry.house, entry.category, entry.subCategory, entry.position,
    +                  entry.points, entry.event, entry.note, entry.date, entry.exam]);
    + return {success:true, ids, count: ids.length, skipped};

### 3) addStudents() — sanitise each row and skip empty names/houses

    - sheet.appendRow([student.name, student.house, student.cls||'', ..., student.total||0, ...]);
    + const student = cleanStudent(raw);
    + if(!student.name || !student.house) { skipped++; return; }
    + sheet.appendRow([student.name, student.house, student.cls, student.sec,
    +                  JSON.stringify(student.subjects), student.total, student.exam, student.date]);

### 4) New upsertStudents() + rewritten importExcelData() (replaces old importExcelData)

  upsertStudents():  Instead of blindly appending, match existing student rows on
  (name | house | class | exam) and UPDATE them in place. Never deletes unrelated rows.

    + const existingByKey = {};          // "name|house|class|exam" -> row index
    + students.forEach(raw => {
    +   const s = cleanStudent(raw);
    +   if(!s.name || !s.house) { skipped++; return; }
    +   const key = [s.name, s.house, s.cls, s.exam].join('|');
    +   if(existingByKey[key]) {
    +     sheet.getRange(rowIdx,5,1,4).setValues([[subjects,total,exam,date]]); // update
    +     updated++;
    +   } else {
    +     sheet.appendRow([...]);          // insert
    +     added++;
    +   }
    + });

  importExcelData():  sanitise + validate the payload, appends entries, merges students.

    + Logger.log(...)  validation logging before any write.
    + const cleanEntries  = (entries||[]).filter(valid house + numeric points);
    + const cleanStudents = (students||[]).map(cleanStudent).filter(name && house);
    + addEntries(cleanEntries);
    + upsertStudents(cleanStudents);

----------------------------------------------------------------------

=== FILE 2: house-tracker.html ===

### 1) computeAcademicRanking() — never let a '-'/NaN/'' student total corrupt a house average

    (entry-based cell accumulation)
    - d.avgSum += parseFloat(m[1]);
    + const mAvg = parseFloat(m[1]);
    + d.avgSum += isNaN(mAvg) ? 0 : mAvg;

    (studentData-based cell accumulation)
    - d.avgSum += s.total || 0;
    + const t = Number(s.total);
    + d.avgSum += isNaN(t) ? 0 : t;   // never let '-'/NaN/'' corrupt the house average

### 2) House detail academic table — show 0 instead of "-" for a missing subject mark

    - const val = s.subjects[sub];
    - if(val === undefined) return `<td ...>-</td>`;
    + const rawVal = s.subjects[sub];
    + const val = (rawVal===undefined || rawVal===null || isNaN(Number(rawVal))) ? 0 : Number(rawVal);

